diff --git a/debian/patches/0904-libvmaf-cuda-accept-10-12-16-bit.patch b/debian/patches/0904-libvmaf-cuda-accept-10-12-16-bit.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0c64faf
--- /dev/null
+++ b/debian/patches/0904-libvmaf-cuda-accept-10-12-16-bit.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+Accept 10-, 12- and 16-bit input in the libvmaf_cuda filter.
+
+libvmaf_cuda rejected everything except 8-bit yuv420p and yuv444p16, so any
+10-bit source -- which is every HDR and Dolby Vision source this fork exists
+to encode -- died at config time with
+
+    Unsupported input format: yuv420p10le
+    Task finished with error code: -22 (Invalid argument)
+
+Nothing behind that check needed changing. pix_fmt_map() already maps all
+twelve of the CPU filter's formats, including AV_PIX_FMT_YUV420P10LE; bpc is
+read straight off the format with desc->comp[0].depth; the device copy sizes
+itself as w * ((bpc + 7) / 8); and libvmaf's CUDA backend accepts bpc 8-16
+(picture_cuda.c: `if (bpc < 8 || bpc > 16) return -EINVAL;`) with every
+feature extractor parameterised on the actual bpc value. The list was simply
+narrower than the code behind it.
+
+So this makes supported_formats[] match the CPU filter's pix_fmts[] exactly.
+Both lists now cover 4:4:4 / 4:2:2 / 4:2:0 at 8, 10, 12 and 16 bit, which is
+also precisely the set pix_fmt_map() understands.
+
+Semi-planar formats are deliberately NOT added. p010 stores luma MSB-aligned
+(value << 6) while desc->comp[0].depth still reports 10, so libvmaf would read
+it 64x too bright and return a plausible, wrong score rather than an error.
+Feed p010 through scale_cuda=format=yuv420p10 instead.
+
+This depends on the libvmaf motion-stride fix carried by
+builder/scripts.d/55-libvmaf.sh. Without it, 10-bit is accepted and scores
+~1.06 VMAF low -- see docs/patches/0009-libvmaf-cuda-10bit.md.
+
+--- a/libavfilter/vf_libvmaf.c
++++ b/libavfilter/vf_libvmaf.c
+@@ -633,8 +633,10 @@
+ 
+ #if CONFIG_LIBVMAF_CUDA_FILTER
+ static const enum AVPixelFormat supported_formats[] = {
+-    AV_PIX_FMT_YUV420P,
+-    AV_PIX_FMT_YUV444P16,
++    AV_PIX_FMT_YUV444P,     AV_PIX_FMT_YUV422P,     AV_PIX_FMT_YUV420P,
++    AV_PIX_FMT_YUV444P10LE, AV_PIX_FMT_YUV422P10LE, AV_PIX_FMT_YUV420P10LE,
++    AV_PIX_FMT_YUV444P12LE, AV_PIX_FMT_YUV422P12LE, AV_PIX_FMT_YUV420P12LE,
++    AV_PIX_FMT_YUV444P16LE, AV_PIX_FMT_YUV422P16LE, AV_PIX_FMT_YUV420P16LE,
+ };
+ 
+ static int format_is_supported(enum AVPixelFormat fmt)
